      "value": "B-AAC - BACnet Advanced Application Controller"
    },
    "productDescription": {
      "provenance": "user-entered",
      "value": "A BACnet/IP device built on the CAS BACnet Stack that implements as much of the B-AAC profile as the stack supports today. It presents three read-only sensor objects, three commandable output objects, an alarm-capable Analog Value with an intrinsic OutOfRange algorithm, the Notification Class that routes its alarms (with a writable Recipient_List), an internal Schedule that writes a target object on a weekly basis and on the dates in a stack-held Calendar, and the required Network Port. It answers ReadProperty / ReadPropertyMultiple, accepts WriteProperty / WritePropertyMultiple, AcknowledgeAlarm, DeviceCommunicationControl, ReinitializeDevice and time synchronization (which sets the device clock that Local_Date / Local_Time report and the Schedule and Calendar follow), and is discoverable by Who-Is / I-Am and Who-Has / I-Have. It is a tutorial for implementers of the B-AAC profile. Its Wire Tests prove the profile's function against a Python operator workstation: a confirmed alarm reaches the recipient a Recipient_List write names, is acknowledged (a stale time stamp is refused with invalid-timestamp), stays listed by GetEventInformation until acknowledged, is retransmitted 3 times (Number_Of_APDU_Retries) to a silent recipient, and is silenced by DCC disable-initiation; a time sync moves the Schedule and Calendar."
    },
    "productName": {
      "provenance": "user-entered",
      "value": "CAS BACnet Stack Example - B-AAC"
    },
